.TH GOS 1 "" "gos" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gos \- install and switch Go versions in seconds
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gos
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
gos (Go Switch) is a single Bash script that installs and switches Go
versions. It downloads the official binary from go.dev, verifies its
SHA256 checksum, installs it transactionally, and can roll back. It needs
nothing but \fBcurl\fR (or \fBwget\fR) and \fBbash\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gos latest
\&Install the latest stable Go version
.TP
.B gos install <version>
\&Install a specific Go version
.TP
.B gos rollback [\-\-dry-run]
\&Restore the previous Go installation, if available; \-\-dry-run only previews the swap
.TP
.B gos uninstall <version or \-\-inactive> [\-\-dry-run]
\&Remove an installed version (side-by-side mode); \-\-inactive removes all but the active and rollback
.TP
.B gos use [\-\-print [\-\-json]] [path]
\&Install the Go version requested by .go-version, .tool-versions, or go.mod; \-\-print only resolves it
.TP
.B gos pin [version]
\&Write .go-version in the current directory (active version by default)
.TP
.B gos run [version] [\-\-] <command> [args...]
\&Run a command with a side-by-side Go version without activating it globally; a bare \-\- uses the project version
.TP
.B gos each <v1,v2,...> [\-\-] <command> [args...]
\&Run a command against several side-by-side Go versions and report a pass/fail summary
.TP
.B gos check [\-\-json]
\&Check whether newer stable Go or gos releases are available (no install)
.TP
.B gos current [\-\-json]
\&Show the currently active Go version
.TP
.B gos list [\-\-installed] [\-\-minor] [\-\-json]
\&List available Go versions (or locally installed ones); \-\-minor keeps the newest per minor
.TP
.B gos platforms [version] [\-\-json]
\&List supported OS/arch archives for a Go version
.TP
.B gos status [\-\-json]
\&Show an offline dashboard for gos and the active Go
.TP
.B gos which [version] [\-\-json]
\&Show the active or side-by-side Go binary path
.TP
.B gos prune [\-\-rollback] [\-\-dry-run] [\-\-json]
\&Remove cached Go archives; \-\-rollback also removes the rollback copy, \-\-dry-run only previews
.TP
.B gos doctor [\-\-fix] [\-\-json]
\&Diagnose gos, Go, PATH, and local tool dependencies; \-\-fix creates safe missing directories and prints the shell setup line
.TP
.B gos env [\-\-fish] [\-\-auto] [\-\-json]
\&Print the PATH setup line or an opt-in per-shell auto-switch hook
.TP
.B gos completions <shell> [\-\-install]
\&Print a Bash, Zsh, or Fish completion script (or install it with \-\-install)
.TP
.B gos self-update
\&Update gos itself to the latest verified release
.TP
.B gos version [\-\-json]
\&Show gos version
.TP
.B gos help [command]
\&Show this help message, or usage for one command
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GOS_INSTALL_DIR
\&Where Go gets installed. Override to install without sudo. Path basename must contain "go". Default: /usr/local/go.
.TP
.B GOS_VERSIONS_DIR
\&Opt-in side-by-side layout (e.g. $HOME/.gos/versions). Each version installs to $GOS_VERSIONS_DIR/go<version> and GOS_INSTALL_DIR becomes a symlink to the active one, so switching is instant. The versions root must not be /, equal to, or inside GOS_INSTALL_DIR. Requires symlink support (macOS, Linux, WSL). Default: unset.
.TP
.B GOS_CACHE_DIR
\&Where verified Go archives, resumable partial downloads, and discovery-only feed metadata are cached. Must be an absolute path. Clear it with gos prune. Default: $XDG_CACHE_HOME/gos or $HOME/.cache/gos.
.TP
.B GOS_DOWNLOAD_MIRROR
\&HTTPS base URL to download Go archives from (e.g. https://golang.google.cn/dl behind restrictive networks). Checksums are still resolved from go.dev, and mirror downloads fail closed when they cannot be verified. Default: unset.
.TP
.B GOS_REQUIRE_CHECKSUM
\&Set to 1 to abort installs when checksum metadata or local SHA256 calculation is unavailable. Set to feed to additionally require the digest to come from the go.dev downloads feed (cross-origin), rejecting the same-origin .sha256 fallback. Honored by gos, install.sh, and install.ps1. Both installers treat feed like 1; install.ps1 rejects unverified main installs under either strict policy. Default: unset.
.TP
.B GOS_FEED_TTL
\&Non-negative integer seconds that discovery commands (list, platforms, check, bare-minor resolution, shell completion suggestions) may reuse cached feed metadata. Set to 0 to disable. Invalid values fail before remote discovery and are reported by gos doctor; checksum verification always fetches fresh metadata. Default: 600.
.TP
.B GOS_NO_COLOR
\&Set to 1 to disable interactive color and symbol styling. Default: unset.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
\&The standard no-color convention: when set to a non-empty value, color and symbols are disabled (same as GOS_NO_COLOR=1). Default: unset.
.TP
.B TERM
\&TERM=dumb disables color and symbols; output is never colored when it is not a terminal or under \-\-json. Default: from the terminal.
.TP
.B GOTOOLCHAIN
\&Read only by gos doctor, which explains how a per-module toolchain composes with the go gos manages on PATH. Default: unset.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
\&Base of the default GOS_CACHE_DIR. Default: $HOME/.cache.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
\&Where gos completions bash \-\-install and zsh \-\-install write their files (bash-completion/completions/gos, zsh/site-functions/_gos). Default: $HOME/.local/share.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
\&Where gos completions fish \-\-install writes fish/completions/gos.fish. Default: $HOME/.config.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a generic failure, 2 for invalid arguments or configuration, 3 when a download or feed fetch failed, 4 when a checksum or release could not be verified, and 5 when another gos holds the mutation lock. With \fB\-\-json\fR a failed command prints one {"error":{"code":...,"message":...}} document on standard output. The doctor command keeps its diagnostic report and exits 1 when it reports problems; invalid doctor arguments still produce a usage error document.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR go (1)
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/johnny4young/gos
